{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778195324,"nonce":"+GzdUuwbjnfEyb7dmBciZxXhNuU=","title":"Move analysis layer into feedbax: Controller protocol, graph-step adapter, LTV/LTI linearisation + induced-gain","message":"**Status:** analysis-only research filing; does NOT propose immediate implementation. Surfaced from rlrmp `74bfd86` design discussion and `53b5fe5` adapter rewrite.\n\n**Background.** rlrmp currently has the linearisation-and-induced-gain machinery in `src/rlrmp/analysis/induced_gain.py` (~1800 LOC) and `src/rlrmp/analysis/hinf_riccati.py` (~1500 LOC). Some of this is feedbax-generic (`Controller` protocol, `feedbax_graph_controller` adapter, LTV trajectory linearisation, power-iteration H∞ norm); some is rlrmp-specific (Riccati solver tuned to point-mass dynamics, channel sentinels named for motor-control concepts, cost-schedule helpers tied to rlrmp's loss config schema).\n\nWith the recent `Graph.step` public API (`0ec8492` / commit `d7616e0`), the feedbax-generic pieces become liftable cleanly.\n\n**Move-vs-stay categorisation** (per analysis subagent investigation):\n\n**Move to feedbax (feedbax-generic):**\n- `Controller` Protocol (`step(h, sensory_obs, t) -\u003e (h_next, u)`; ~30 LOC, no rlrmp deps)\n- `_FeedbaxGraphController` + `feedbax_graph_controller` adapter (~100 LOC, depends only on now-public `Graph.step` / `Graph.initial_cycle_port_values`)\n- `TrajectoryLinearisation` / `FixedPointLinearisation` data containers (~90 LOC, generic named tuples for `(A_t, Bw_t, Cz_t, Dz_t)`)\n- `linearise_trajectory` core (rolls a nominal reach, computes Jacobians via autodiff; works on any Controller)\n- Power-iteration algorithm (`induced_gain_power_iteration`; fully generic, takes `(A_t, Bw_t, Cz_t, Dz_t)` arrays)\n- `_flatten_pytree_to_array` / `_unflatten_array_to_pytree` JAX PyTree utilities (could go to `feedbax._tree` or `jax_cookbook`)\n\n**rlrmp-specific but lifts cleanly with abstraction work:**\n- `linearize_pointmass` — point-mass-specific, but pattern (continuous-time → ZOH discretise) generalises; feedbax version would be `linearize_dynamical_system(model, x0, u0)` via JAX autodiff\n- `linearize_from_model` — walks `SimpleFeedback` to extract plant params; pattern generalises\n- `PlantLinearization` — currently carries pos/vel/force slices; needs to generalise or specialise\n\n**Stay in rlrmp (rlrmp-specific):**\n- `CostSpec`, `cost_schedule_from_spec`, `cost_schedule_from_loss_config` — hardwired to rlrmp loss config schema\n- `solve_hinf_riccati`, `solve_lqr`, `find_gamma_star` — Riccati solver; mathematically general but Q/R shapes and `CostSchedule` rlrmp-tuned\n- `simulate_closed_loop`, `compute_velocity_inflation` — rlrmp reach simulation, C\u0026S comparison metric\n- Channel sentinels (`W_ADDITIVE_FORCE`, etc.) — named for motor-control concepts\n- Hamiltonian bisection (`induced_gain_hamiltonian`) — depends on `solve_hinf_riccati`'s `_bounded_real_admissible`; would need splitting\n\n**Open design questions** (require user judgement before implementation):\n1. **Linearisation API shape.** Autodiff-based `linearize_at_point(model, x0, u0, dt) -\u003e (A, B)` is the feedbax-natural pattern; rlrmp's analytical `linearize_pointmass` derives matrices from first-principles ODE knowledge. Both valid; pick one as the primary feedbax API.\n2. **`Controller` Protocol shape.** Current rlrmp protocol takes `(h: Array, obs: Array, t: int)`. Feedbax-generic could use `Graph` state directly or accept `ModelInput`. Needs commitment.\n3. **`PlantLinearization` generalisation.** Currently hardwires 2D pos/vel/force slices. Generic version: drop named slices and use raw `(A, B, Bw, dt)`, or support user-supplied slice map.\n4. **Namespace.** `feedbax.analysis` does not exist. Where does this live?\n5. **`jax_enable_x64` side effect.** Both rlrmp modules set `jax_enable_x64` at import time. Lifting into feedbax library means callers may not expect this side effect.\n\n**Cost estimate:**\n- Moving the adapter alone (Controller protocol + feedbax_graph_controller): **S** (~200 LOC; well-tested; clear target API on develop).\n- Moving generic LTV/LTI machinery (linearise_*, power iteration): **M** (~600 LOC core; design effort on `PlantLinearization` generalisation).\n- Full analysis layer with generalised linearisation API: **L** (commits to `analysis/` namespace, autodiff-vs-analytical decision, Controller protocol commitment).\n\n**Recommended phasing:**\n1. Phase 1 (S): adapter only. Move `Controller` protocol + `feedbax_graph_controller` + `_flatten_pytree_to_array` helpers. No design questions; just relocation. rlrmp imports the adapter from feedbax; `feedbax_graph_controller` becomes a public part of feedbax's API.\n2. Phase 2 (M): linearisation containers + LTV linearisation + power iteration. Defers the autodiff-vs-analytical question by keeping the linearisation function signature `linearise_trajectory(plant, controller, ...)` where `plant` is a domain-specific structure (rlrmp continues providing `PlantLinearization` for point-mass; feedbax adds optional autodiff-based path).\n3. Phase 3 (L): generic linearisation API + Hamiltonian extraction + namespace decision. Substantial design work; punt until phases 1–2 stabilise.\n\n**Connection to recent work.** The recent `Graph.step` API is the prerequisite for phase 1. With that landed, phase 1 is unblocked.\n\n**Cross-refs.** rlrmp `74bfd86` (induced-gain analyser; the canonical design spec); rlrmp `53b5fe5` (the adapter rewrite that exercises Graph.step); rlrmp meta coord `1d9ae6f` (this issue cross-linked there); feedbax `0ec8492` (the Graph.step prerequisite that landed).","files":null}]}